From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: recore: drop the preboot= that Armbian's splash patch defines

Armbian carries patch/u-boot/u-boot-sunxi/allwinner-boot-splash.patch, which
adds a splash loader and, as a side effect, defines preboot:

	#ifdef CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD
	#if defined CONFIG_VIDEO
	#define CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS \
		"preboot=run loadsplash; usb start\0" \
		"stdin=serial,usbkbd\0"

Both conditions hold on Recore - CONFIG_VIDEO=y from recore_defconfig, and
CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD=y inherited from the sunxi defaults - so that preboot is
real, and it collides with ours.

recore_defconfig sets CONFIG_PREBOOT to
"mw.l 0x01f01400 0x00020102; usb reset; run bootcmd_usb0", which is what boots
the board from USB for Reflash. Both definitions land in the same default
environment blob - CONFIG_PREBOOT via env_default.h:63, theirs via
CFG_EXTRA_ENV_SETTINGS at env_default.h:119 - and which one survives depends on
U-Boot's duplicate-key handling during env import. That is not a detail the USB
boot path should rest on, so remove theirs and leave exactly one definition.

Nothing of value is lost. Their loadsplash does "load mmc 0 ... boot.bmp",
which cannot work when booting from USB; ours is in
userpatches/bootscripts/boot-sun50i-next.cmd, uses ${devtype}/${devnum}, is
guarded so a missing image cannot break boot, and can be turned off with
splashfile= in armbianEnv.txt. The other half of their patch is welcome and
kept: CMD_BMP defaulting to y, and the CONFIG_SPLASH_*/CONFIG_BMP_* defines
(all of which recore_defconfig also sets explicitly).

This replaces deleting the whole Armbian patch from the build tree in
rebuild.sh, which is what we used to do. Patches are applied in alphabetical
order by filename, so "allwinner-boot-splash.patch" is applied before
"u-boot-sunxi64-legacy-*", and this can simply build on top of it.

Only the preboot line is removed. The two CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS branches are
left identical rather than collapsing the now-redundant #if, to keep the diff
against Armbian's patch as small as possible - the smaller it is, the less
likely it is to conflict when they touch that file.

Signed-off-by: Elias Bakken <elias@iagent.no>
---
 include/configs/sunxi-common.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -303,7 +303,6 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_KEYBOARD
 #if defined CONFIG_VIDEO
 #define CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS \
-	"preboot=run loadsplash; usb start\0" \
 	"stdin=serial,usbkbd\0"
 #else
 #define CONSOLE_STDIN_SETTINGS \
